{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Design Patterns"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about design patterns in Software Engineering."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives With Irregular Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use comparatives to show differences between two or more elements."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In our last survey of customer support system, there were fewer positive results than two months ago. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If these ones aren't solved on time, it could be worse than solving the big ones afterward."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's better to implement this solution than other complex ones."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, there are regular and irregular adjectives. Regarding regular adjectives, there are clear rules to establish their comparison, such as <i>er</i> or <i>ier</i>. <br><br>  On the other hand, irregular adjectives don't follow exact rules since they have different changes.<br><br><center>  Subject + verb + <b>irregular adjective + than </b>+ complement<br><br></center>  Examples: <br><i> This design pattern is <b>better than</b> that other one.<br> The performance of this application is <b>worse than</b> the previous ones.<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">IRREGULAR ADJECTIVES</span></div>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Good/ Well</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Better</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Bad</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Worse</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Far </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Farther/ Further</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Little</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Less</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Many/ Much</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">More</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Old\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><b>Older/elder\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Possessive Pronouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use <span class=\"italic\">Possessive Pronouns</span> to indicate the possession of something. In English, for each subject pronoun there's a <span class=\"italic\">Possessive Pronoun.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " A <span class=\"italic\">Possessive Pronoun</span> replaces a noun phrase.</br></br>  <span class=\"italic\">Possessive pronouns are: mine, yours, his, hers, its, ours and theirs.</span></br></br>  Check the chart below with examples for each subject pronoun:</br></br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"strong\">POSSESSIVE PRONOUNS</span></div>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject Pronoun</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Possessive Pronoun</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><b>Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">I</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Mine</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-Is this your design? <br> \u2013Yes, It's <b>mine.</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">You</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Yours</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-I found this report in my desk, is it <b>yours</b>?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">He</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">His</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-I bet this computer belongs to John.<br> -No, it doesn't. This one is blue and <b>his</b> is red\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">She</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Hers</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-Whose book is this? </br> -Let me check, maybe it's my sister's. Oh\u2026yes, it's <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hers</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">We</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Ours</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-Hey, the software is <b>ours.</b><br> -Don't touch it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">They</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Theirs</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-I love the design Karen and David create. <br> -I prefer Cindy and Christian's. Even though <b>theirs</b> is good too.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have got this report about some problems that occur with                our software design, is this yours?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yes, sir. It's mine."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "request"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a petition done by a user"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Users complain that they don't receive an immediate response to their requests."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pattern "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a scheme to follow for solving a coding problem"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We must implement design patterns."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "subtle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " imperceptible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This solution must be reusable or at least to have a variant that can figure out other problems as subtle issues."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "speed up    "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to perform a task quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Design patterns could speed up and improve development software processes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coder  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a programmer in the computing field"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Coders and architects have got the possibility to improve their code readability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "training"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the development of particular skills before making an activity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As software engineers they have got a lot of training in this practice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about a possible design problem you had or could have. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Plan the way you would solve that problem using a design pattern."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your plan to a partner and ask for suggestions."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think about possible software design problems"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  plan a design pattern to solve the problem"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my plan to a partner and receive suggestions"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n4le01ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: Good morning, Helen!<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Good morning, Mr. Dawson!<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: Can you please come to my office?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Yes, Sir.<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: I have this report about some problems that occur with our software design, is this yours?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Yes, sir. It's mine.<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: So, I'm all ears.<br>\n<b>Helen:</b>Indeed, we have got some software design problems. In our last survey of customer support system, there were fewer positive results than two months ago. Users complain that they don't receive an immediate response to their requests. This is due to some weaknesses in the software system. On the other hand, we need to create a chat application so they can communicate with each other."}, {"time": "40000", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: What do you suggest?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b>We must implement design patterns, which are very important tools in software design. They can be descriptions or templates that solve the most common problems in software design. Such solutions must be reusable, or at least need to have a variant that can figure out other problems as subtle issues. Because if these ones aren't solved on time, it could be worse than solving the big ones afterward. For that reason, design patterns could speed up and improve our software development process.<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: You're right. It's better to implement this solution than other complex ones.<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Exactly."}, {"time": "78000", "image": "enpe8n4le01ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: What other advantages do design patterns offer?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Coders and architects have got the possibility to improve their code readability.<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: How does it work?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> It works on different sections, such as participants, collaboration, and structures.<br>\n<b>Mr. Dawson</b>: Have our engineers got the appropriate experience on that? Or, do we have to hire engineers with more experience than theirs?<br>\n<b>Helen:</b> Of course, as software engineers, they have got a lot of training in this practice."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n4le01ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 4, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about commonly occurring problems in software design. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what design patterns are."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can ask questions related to design patterns in software engineering."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How could you define a design pa